<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Southbrook Kitchen 3D Configurator — v19.0.4.21.0
  Canonical catalog overlay.

  Tags the 12 CLAUDE.md-locked cabinet templates (owned by
  southbrook_estimating) so the 3D Configurator's inventory pane
  can see them. Without this overlay, the estimating templates
  are invisible to the configurator (which searches
  product_template_id.southbrook_is_cabinet = True) and the
  inventory falls back to only the 7 demo cabinets in
  data/demo_cabinets.xml. Audit 2026-07-01 (§6.2) flagged this
  as the P0 catalog integration gap.

  Why the overlay lives here, not in southbrook_estimating:
    southbrook_kitchen_3d_configurator depends on
    southbrook_estimating (per CLAUDE.md §3 — estimating is the
    OCA foundation, configurator sits on top). The
    `southbrook_is_cabinet` field is defined by
    southbrook_kitchen_3d_configurator/models/product_template.py.
    Adding the field to estimating's product_templates.xml would
    reference a field that doesn't exist yet at estimating install
    time — install would fail. The overlay pattern loads AFTER
    estimating so the ref lookups resolve and the fields are
    already in the ORM.

  Two of the 12 canonicals are handled specially:

    * `worktop` — NOT tagged. It's a countertop / surface product,
      not a cabinet. None of the 6 valid cabinet_type values
      (base/wall/tall/filler/panel/corner) fits. PRODBOARD_MANIFEST
      §4.3 / §5.1 documents worktop as its own module class with a
      length-based dimension model, distinct from carcasses.

    * `accessory` — tagged with cabinet_type=panel as a fallback.
      The canonical `accessory` template carries a sub-attribute
      `accessory_type: end_panel/filler/cornice/pelmet/plinth` per
      CLAUDE.md §3, so it's really a container for 5 different
      product classes. "panel" is the least-wrong single type;
      accessory-with-filler variants render correctly regardless.

  Dimensions:
    * `southbrook_width_in` is set to the MIDPOINT of each
      template's width envelope (per Southbrook_Excel_to_Odoo_
      Mapping §3.1). Width on the canonicals is a VARIANT
      attribute (attr_width value_ids in product_templates.xml),
      not a scalar — so template-level southbrook_width_in is a
      fallback the configurator uses when no variant is picked.
      Follow-up P1: compute variant-level southbrook_width_in
      from product_template_attribute_value_ids so each variant
      reports its true width.
    * `southbrook_height_in` and `southbrook_depth_in` are
      NA-cabinetry standards. None of the four canonical docs
      specifies per-template H/D — the audit agent inferred them
      from convention. If Southbrook's Consolidated Dataset
      differs, override here.

  Retirement path for the 7 demo cabinets in data/demo_cabinets.xml:
    Deferred — no name/default_code/xmlid collision exists (audit
    confirmed), so both catalogs can coexist. Semantic overlap is
    real (e.g. "B24 Base Cabinet" vs "Base 2-Door" width=24)
    but not broken. Retire demos in a future clean-up sprint
    once the canonical variants ship variant-aware widths.

  noupdate="0" so a bump of this addon re-applies the tags —
  guards against accidental UI edits (or a Studio user) that
  clears the flag on a template.
-->
<odoo noupdate="0">

  <!-- Wall cabinets ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <record id="southbrook_estimating.wall_1dr" model="product.template">
    <field name="southbrook_is_cabinet" eval="True"/>
    <field name="southbrook_cabinet_type">wall</field>
    <field name="southbrook_width_in">15</field>
    <field name="southbrook_height_in">30</field>
    <field name="southbrook_depth_in">12</field>
    <field name="sale_ok" eval="True"/>
  </record>

  <record id="southbrook_estimating.wall_2dr" model="product.template">
    <field name="southbrook_is_cabinet" eval="True"/>
    <field name="southbrook_cabinet_type">wall</field>
    <field name="southbrook_width_in">30</field>
    <field name="southbrook_height_in">30</field>
    <field name="southbrook_depth_in">12</field>
    <field name="sale_ok" eval="True"/>
  </record>

  <!-- Base cabinets ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <record id="southbrook_estimating.base_1dr" model="product.template">
